-- Independent tests for the Israeli Interpretation Law 5741-1981 and the Interpretation Ordinance [New Version].
-- Expected values come from ANSWERS.md in the review directory, written from the Hebrew text BEFORE any .l4 file was opened.
-- Scenario numbers S### are ANSWERS.md's. A scenario the encoding has no function for is a GAP (listed in triage.md), not invented here.
-- Where ANSWERS.md says NOT COVERED the assertion is #ASSERT REFUSED, the encoding's own convention for "the text does not say".

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Helpers: facts the tests supply`

-- Rest-day calendars. The Law leaves which days are days of rest to other enactments (ANSWERS.md conventions);
-- a holiday set is IN ADDITION to Saturdays.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays only` MEANS `Weekday of` d EQUALS 6

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays and Fri 2021-03-05` MEANS `Weekday of` d EQUALS 6 OR d EQUALS (YMD 2021 3 5)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays and Mon 2021-03-15` MEANS `Weekday of` d EQUALS 6 OR d EQUALS (YMD 2021 3 15)

`a Knesset law` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS TRUE, `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE
`a Mandate-era ordinance` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS TRUE, `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE
`a Provisional Council ordinance` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS TRUE
`no statute` MEANS `A candidate statute` WITH `passed by the Knesset as a law` IS FALSE, `an ordinance given before the establishment of the State` IS FALSE, `an ordinance of the Provisional Council of State` IS FALSE

GIVEN direction IS A BOOLEAN
      inWriting IS A BOOLEAN
      legislative IS A BOOLEAN
      byVirtue IS A MAYBE `A candidate statute`
GIVETH AN Instrument
`test instrument` MEANS Instrument WITH `taken as a statute` IS `no statute`, `the statute it was given by virtue of` IS byVirtue, `of legislative effect` IS legislative, `given in writing` IS inWriting, `a direction or appointment, or a notice, announcement, licence, permit or the like` IS direction, `a direction` IS FALSE, `an appointment` IS FALSE, `a notice` IS FALSE, `an announcement` IS FALSE, `a licence` IS FALSE, `a permit` IS FALSE, `something like them` IS FALSE

`a statute as an instrument` MEANS Instrument WITH `taken as a statute` IS `a Knesset law`, `the statute it was given by virtue of` IS NOTHING, `of legislative effect` IS FALSE, `given in writing` IS TRUE, `a direction or appointment, or a notice, announcement, licence, permit or the like` IS FALSE, `a direction` IS FALSE, `an appointment` IS FALSE, `a notice` IS FALSE, `an announcement` IS FALSE, `a licence` IS FALSE, `a permit` IS FALSE, `something like them` IS FALSE

GIVEN ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      presents IS A BOOLEAN
      visible IS A BOOLEAN
      decodable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A presentation of letters, numerals or signs`
`law writing` MEANS `A presentation of letters, numerals or signs` WITH `it is writing in the ordinary sense` IS ordinary, `it presents letters, numerals or signs` IS presents, `in a form visible to the eye` IS visible, `in a form capable of being decoded visually` IS decodable, `it presents letters` IS FALSE, `it presents numerals` IS FALSE, `it presents signs` IS FALSE

GIVEN isCourt IS A BOOLEAN
      lies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A judgment or decision`
`a judgment` MEANS `A judgment or decision` WITH `it is a judgment or decision of a court` IS isCourt, `an appeal, objection or the like still lies against it` IS lies, `an appeal still lies against it` IS FALSE, `an appeal by petition still lies against it` IS FALSE, `an objection still lies against it` IS FALSE, `a like remedy still lies against it` IS FALSE

GIVEN tangible IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A BOOLEAN
      built IS A BOOLEAN
      planted IS A BOOLEAN
      attached IS A BOOLEAN
      detachable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A thing of property`
`a thing` MEANS `A thing of property` WITH `it is tangible` IS tangible, `it is ground` IS ground, `it is built on ground` IS built, `it is planted in ground` IS planted, `it is attached to ground permanently` IS attached, `it is a detachable fixture` IS detachable

GIVEN ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      useful IS A BOOLEAN
      employee IS A BOOLEAN
      guarding IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A holding of land`
`a holding under the Law` MEANS `A holding of land` WITH `it is possession in the ordinary sense` IS ordinary, `it is use, possession or enjoyment` IS useful, `it is as an employee or official only` IS employee, `it is for supervision or guarding only` IS guarding, `it is use` IS FALSE, `it is possession` IS FALSE, `it is enjoyment` IS FALSE

GIVEN legal IS A BOOLEAN
      obligations IS A BOOLEAN
      rights IS A BOOLEAN
      acts IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A body`
`a body` MEANS `A body` WITH `it is a legal body` IS legal, `it is capable of obligations` IS obligations, `it is capable of rights` IS rights, `it is capable of legal acts` IS acts

GIVEN written IS A BOOLEAN
      given IS A BOOLEAN
      verified IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A declaration`
`a declaration` MEANS `A declaration` WITH `it is a declaration in writing` IS written, `it was given` IS given, `it was verified in one of the ways an enactment fixes for it` IS verified

GIVEN seaward IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A point at sea`
`a point at sea` MEANS `A point at sea` WITH `it is in the open sea along the coast of the State` IS TRUE, `its distance seaward from the low-water point on the shore, in nautical miles` IS seaward

GIVEN prosecutor IS A BOOLEAN
      authorised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A person who may represent the Attorney General`
`a would-be representative` MEANS `A person who may represent the Attorney General` WITH `a prosecutor in the State Attorney's Office, including its branches` IS prosecutor, `authorised by the Attorney General to be his representative or agent` IS authorised

GIVEN hebrewStart IS A BOOLEAN
      hebrewEnd IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Specification of a period of years or months`
`a period specified` MEANS `Specification of a period of years or months` WITH `beginning by the Hebrew calendar only` IS hebrewStart, `end by the Hebrew calendar only` IS hebrewEnd

-- s 2: a use of a defined term.
GIVEN where IS A `Where a defined term is used`
      form IS A `The form a defined term takes`
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      inconsistent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A use of a defined term`
`a use of the term` MEANS `A use of a defined term` WITH `where it is used` IS where, `the form it takes` IS form, `another provision deals with the matter` IS other, `something in the matter or its context is inconsistent with that definition` IS inconsistent

§§ `A. The gate (Law ss 1-2)`

