-- RECONCILED S013: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1)`; triaged against the text: the reviewer's own ambiguity: a statute given exactly on the Law's commencement day; a day-level date cannot say whether it was given before 00:01 that day, so the module refuses (Law s.1 L22, s.21 L124, s.32 L162)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — section 3 applies to` `the word day` `in an enactment given on` (YMD 1981 10 1)  -- S013 [Law s.1 L22, s.32 L162] (AMBIG(Y), my pick: the commencement day counts as not-before)
-- S014, S015, S016, S017, S018, S021: GAP (the Law's reach by statute date for ss 4-26, and by kind of instrument, is not a function)
