§§ `E. Law Part C (ss 11-20): powers`

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE `A version of an enactment's wording`
GIVETH A STRING
`the wording of` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN "(no wording in force)"
    WHEN JUST v THEN v's `wording`

`a power with no time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH `its kind` IS `an authorisation`, `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS FALSE
`a duty with no time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH `its kind` IS `an obligation`, `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS FALSE
`a duty with a time fixed` MEANS `An authorisation or obligation to do a thing` WITH `its kind` IS `an obligation`, `the enactment fixes a time for doing it` IS TRUE

`office holders` MEANS LIST (`A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "A", `from` IS YMD 2020 1 1, `until` IS YMD 2020 12 31), (`A holder of an office` WITH `person` IS "B", `from` IS YMD 2021 1 1, `until` IS YMD 2021 12 31)

GIVEN what IS A `What a power to make rules concerns`
      done IS A `What is done to the regulations or direction`
      inTheWay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction`
`a step on rules` MEANS `A step taken on regulations or on an administrative direction` WITH `what they are` IS what, `what is done to them` IS done, `it is done in the way they were made or given` IS inTheWay

-- s 11
#ASSERT `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `a power with no time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS `a power to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`  -- S214 [Law s.11 L90]
#ASSERT `s 11 — it is to be done again:` `a power with no time fixed` `, the circumstances requiring it:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`  -- S215 [Law s.11 L90]
#ASSERT `s 11 — what the authority amounts to when no time is fixed:` `a duty with no time fixed` `, for` `a matter nothing displaces` EQUALS `a duty to do it with the proper speed, and again from time to time as the circumstances require`  -- S216 [Law s.11 L90]
-- RECONCILED S217: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `a duty with a time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`)`; triaged against the text: Law s.11 (L90) speaks only of an authorisation or obligation for which no time is fixed; the gate refuses for one with a fixed time (design choice, il-interpretation-gate.l4)
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 11 — the thing was done in time:` `a duty with a time fixed` `, the time taken being the proper speed:` TRUE `, for` `a matter nothing displaces`  -- S217 [Law s.11 L90] (expects N; the module may refuse because s 11 does not speak to a fixed time)
-- S218: GAP (no function returns a number of days for "the proper speed"; the module leaves it a judgement input)

