-- ===================== GAPS =====================
-- The test author's list of the scenarios the encoding had no function for when it ran the file (37 scenarios), with its one-line reason at that time.
-- Added by the lead from the test author's report, by script. The fix pass later gave several of them a function; NOTES.md, 'Scenario codes from the independent test pass', says where each of those lands.
-- GAP S014, S015, S021: Law ss.5, 10, 20 apply to a statute of 1960, s.1's carve-out being only of s.3 (Law s.1 L22). The gate functions take two judgements about the matter and no statute date. Only `s 1 — section 3 applies to` takes a date.
-- GAP S016, S017, S018: the Law reaches an administrative instruction; the Ordinance definitions reach one; a private contract is outside (Law s.1 L22, O12). Kind of instrument is not a parameter of any function.
-- GAP S065, S066, S067: the source of the meaning of חטא, עוון, פשע is the Penal Law 5737-1977 (Law s.3 L40, 52, 53). The Penal Law appears only in function names; each function returns its own boolean input.
-- GAP S105: "תפישה" is a rule for land only (Law s.3 L60). The input type is "a holding of land".
-- GAP S188: 1 month after 1 Nisan 5780 (Hebrew calendar) ends 1 Iyar 5780 (Law s.3 L57, s.10(b) L84). No Hebrew-date type; the module refuses Hebrew-calendar arithmetic by design (S642 asserts that refusal).
-- GAP S218: the number of days "due speed" means (Law s.11 L90). No such function; the module makes it a judgement input.
-- GAP S231, S232: an appointment by name alone does not pass to the next holder; by name AND office, s.13(b) does not apply (Law s.13(b) L97). Only a designation by office alone is a function.
-- GAP S269: s.20 does not apply where the enactment requires all to act (Law s.20 L119). The function takes two numbers; no gate.
-- GAP S275, S285: s.22 and s.24 reach every "דין" (Ottoman law included) (Law s.22 L127, s.24 L136). Not a function.
-- GAP S289, S643: s.25 for a private contract / for an administrative instruction (Law s.25 L139). The function takes an enactment.
-- GAP S293: a deviation from a form no enactment prescribed (Law s.26 L142). Not a function.
-- GAP S298: Law s.28 states no operative rule (Law s.28 L150). Only carried as a note string.
-- GAP S321: the Ordinance text is dated 1954-01-01 (O259). Not a value (the module's comment says the signature date is not the publication date).
-- GAP S554: a president of a magistrates' court is covered by the "שופט" extension (Ord s.1 O104). No such office among `A judicial office`.
-- GAP S591, S599, S600, S601: duty to publish in Reshumot; an administrative instruction; never-published regulations; publication only in a newspaper (Ord s.17 O173). s.17's functions take the publication day as given.
-- GAP S631, S632, S633, S634, S636: deemed service; registered mail; a period counted backwards; hours; business days (whole texts). The texts are silent and the module has no function (so no refusal either).
-- GAP S635: which days are statutory rest days (Law s.10(c) L85). An input by design, not a refusal.
-- GAP S637: a foreign State as an "אדם" (Law s.4 L65). The subject type has no such case.
-- GAP S638: schedule or table rows (whole texts). None exist.
-- GAP S639: the text of the definition of "פשע" (Law s.3 L53). Not a value.
-- GAP S641: quorum for a majority act (Law s.20 L119). No function.
